===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|British|intransitive}} To carry out [[physical]] [[labor]] on a [[civil engineering]] [[project]].
#* '''1974''', Malcolm MacDonald, ''World From Rough Stones'', 2013, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=AVcNVUOy52cC&pg=PT709&dq=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=h9PtUpjPOoSUkwX17IDYCA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&f=false unnumbered page],
#*: But by pretending to believe he's '''navvied''' before, I've given him double reason to drive himself hard.
#* '''1978''', [[w:John Shaw Neilson|John Shaw Neilson]], ''The Autobiography of John Shaw Neilson'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=MdTHAQAAQBAJ&pg=PT99&dq=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=h9PtUpjPOoSUkwX17IDYCA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&f=false page 104],
#*: Before my time of '''navvying''' I believe the times were still worse.
#* '''1995''', [[w:F. R. Leavis|F. R. Leavis]], Ian Duncan MacKillop, Richard Storer (editors), ''F.R. Leavis: Essays and Documents'', 2005, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=IYHoy8YohAIC&pg=PA89&dq=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=h9PtUpjPOoSUkwX17IDYCA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22navvying%22%7C%22navvied%22&f=false page 89],
#*: Three terms to use for George Eliot: the feminine imagination and sensibility; Intellect, the capacity for higher '''navvying'''; Intelligence.